{"author":{"id":"a3a282966ced55effb4560271fcd98e13241af24ea76b00ec76a0f18154bc8ee"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790639878,"nonce":"GBpLVBd2a9CIXY5t4LGbcAHymlU=","title":"Views create issues: a ghost + card that opens a new-issue creator","message":"Outcome: every view that lists issues has a place to add one, in the terminal and in the GUI. On a board, a ghost \"+\" card at the foot of each column — and of each lane's column when `group_by` is bound — so that the issue it creates is already where it was added: the `columns` field and the `group_by` field prefilled from where the ghost stands. On a list, a ghost row at the end of each group, prefilling `group_by` the same way. Enter on the ghost opens the creator; the new issue appears where the ghost was, with the cursor on it, through the same refresh every write already triggers.\n\nThe creator itself is the open design question, and the design document (doc/design/\u003cslug\u003e.md, approved before any code, per the working conventions) decides it. Two shapes are on the table:\n\n1. A `new` view kind, `work.view.new(fields={...})` / `git work view new`: show's page over an issue that does not exist yet — a type picker, the title input, the fields table with the prefilled values, the description box — and one button, Create, that commits it and turns the page into show on the created issue. Nothing is written until Create, so an abandoned creation costs nothing; it needs a page that holds a draft.\n\n2. Create, then show: the ghost commits a minimal issue at once (type from the view's query or a picker, a placeholder title, the prefilled fields) and opens show on it, where everything is edited as today. It is one command already (`work.issue.new` then `work.view.show`), and a flow can script it now. What it costs is that an abandoned creation leaves a placeholder issue in the store — the title cannot be cleared, so the undo is an archive — and the schema check runs before a title was typed.\n\nWhatever shape wins is a view, so flows call it and the GUI draws it (two backends of one capability, never a capability on one surface and not the other). Prefilling is what makes the ghost worth having over `git work issue new`: the place it stands is the fields it fills.\n\nTasks: the issues whose parent is this story.","files":null,"fields":{"area":["tui","gui"],"status":"to-do","type":"story"}}]}